name: Explicit zero calls allow finite local discovery and human review without model authority
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/zero_calls.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed @TMP_HOME
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
submit: setg ui.auto_open_viz false
paste-file: @ART/map-command.txt
keys: Enter
submit: map
require-live-snap: 30 RESULT READY | imported-map
nav-mode:
keys: u
require-live-snap: 25 Map ✓ | accepted-map
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/zero_calls.py @TMP_TARGET @ART prepare
submit: campaign owned-zero-calls
require-live-snap: 25 owned-zero-calls | unapproved-plan
nav-mode:
keys: a
require-live-snap: 25 PLAN A STUDY | study-form
keys: Down Down Down Down Down Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Total calls | total-editor
type: 0
keys: Enter Down Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Protected review | review-editor
type: 0
keys: Enter L Home
require-live-snap: 25 REVIEW PLAN & ALLOWANCE | allowance-start
expect: Total provider calls: 0
expect: Protected review calls: 0
require-live-snap: 20 ZERO PROVIDER CALLS | zero-authority
expect: model-assisted Review
expect: Protected Review limit: 0 calls within the total
ask: Does zero clearly forbid all model requests while keeping the three approved local passes and human review available, without silently lowering an existing Review allocation?
resize: 160x48
live-snap: allowance-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: allowance-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: allowance-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: allowance-60x20
resize: 40x12
keys: Home
live-snap: allowance-start-40x12
keys: End
require-live-snap: 20 y approve | allowance-tail-40x12
ask: Are the zero-call terms and exact fixed workload readable through paging at narrow sizes, with approval reachable only after reviewing the document?
resize: 120x36
keys: End y
require-live-snap: 25 Approval saved | approved-zero
keys: L
require-live-snap: 25 L starts its fixed jobs | fixed-jobs
keys: L
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/zero_calls.py @TMP_TARGET @ART completed
keys: r
require-live-snap: 25 3 completed | completed
ask: Do three separate completed local runs show their observations with zero provider calls and no fourth job or implicit model-assisted review?
submit: workbench
require-live-snap: 25 Viewing Scan | scan-result
nav-mode:
keys: n
require-live-snap: 25 Viewing Review | accepted-scan
submit: findings
require-live-snap: 25 FINDINGS · 2 | deduplicated-list
submit: open F-0001
require-live-snap: 25 signal-only | first-review
submit: dismiss false_positive Owned public example is not an active credential
submit: open F-0002
require-live-snap: 25 signal-only | second-review
submit: dismiss false_positive Owned public example is not an active credential
submit: report
require-live-snap: 25 Scope: study owned-zero-calls | report
expect: 0 committed / 0 calls
expect: 2 findings · 0 pending · TP: 0 · FP: 2
expect: 0 pending · 2 FP
resize: 160x48
live-snap: report-decisions-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: report-decisions-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: report-decisions-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: report-decisions-60x20
resize: 40x12
keys: Home
live-snap: report-decisions-40x12
keys: End
live-snap: report-tail-40x12
resize: 120x36
keys: Home
keys: j j j Enter
require-live-snap: 25 EXPORTED | exported
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/zero_calls.py @TMP_TARGET @ART exported
keys: s Home
require-live-snap: 25 0 pending · 2 FP | workspace-history-decisions
expect: Scope: workspace history
keys: r
require-live-snap: 25 0 pending · 2 FP | refreshed-history-decisions
expect: Scope: workspace history
expect: format json (4/6)
expect: 0 pending · 2 FP
keys: s Home
require-live-snap: 25 Scope: study owned-zero-calls | returned-study-decisions
ask: Does export retain six observations, both FP decisions and zero-call accounting, while history and study remain distinct and reopening Report preserves its selected scope and format?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
submit: campaign owned-zero-calls
require-live-snap: 25 3 completed | recovered-jobs
submit: report
require-live-snap: 25 Scope: study owned-zero-calls | recovered-report
expect: 2 findings · 0 pending · TP: 0 · FP: 2
expect: 0 pending · 2 FP
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/zero_calls.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: Does no-color restart preserve the completed plan, zero allowance and both human decisions without restarting work?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
